  "question": {
    "text": "The solution of the differential equation $\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}$ satisfying the condition $y(1)=1$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "8cYd4",
      "text": "\n$y=\\ln x+x$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "09fU5",
      "text": "\n$y=x \\ln x+x^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "jJRfu",
      "text": "\n$y=x e^{(x-1)}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EsH0N",
      "text": "\n$y=x \\ln x+x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\ny=v x\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d y}{d x}=v+x \\frac{d v}{d x} \\\\\n& v+x \\frac{d v}{d x}=1+v \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow d v=\\frac{d x}{x} \\\\\n& \\therefore v=\\log x+c \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{y}{x}=\\log x+c\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSince, $y(1)=1$, we have\n$$\ny=x \\log x+x\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
